            <ArticleTitle>Thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura presenting as a sudden headache with focal neurologic findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura presenting as a sudden headache with associated neurologic deficits. The diagnosis of this rare disorder is discussed, with special attention given to a potential pitfall in evaluation and treatment--platelet transfusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
